  "body": "PR479 checks chirp phases with extensive exact numerical replay. This adds an independent polynomial implementation that executes its pinned `ChirpStream.advance` and checks the full state invariant through ordinary increments, carries and final restoration. **Status: independent verification; no new kappa or source defect claimed.**\n\nThe source-linked symbolic executions cover 27 carry patterns in dimensions 1\u20136 and 587 state equalities. The separate integer checker covers 8,605 states in 129 small boxes and 21 wide transitions at r=2^80. Sixteen source mutations have concrete witnesses; ten also fail symbolically. The six remaining controls expose the congruence model's initialization/canonical-residue boundary. Two equivalent source rewrites pass. A written argument explains arbitrary-dimension composition, without presenting the finite pattern replay as a formal loop proof.\n\nFor a concrete control, replacing the phase increment with A at r=t=4, s=1, j=1 yields phase 6 instead of 4 modulo 8.\n\nReproduce with Python 3.10+ and the standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B -I -O research/chirp-symbolic-seed80/verify.py\npython3 -B -I -O research/chirp-symbolic-seed80/test_verify.py\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_CHIRP_SYMBOLIC_INVARIANTS symbolic=27 identities=587 transitions=8605 controls=16`, then eight passing test groups. Verified on macOS arm64 with Python 3.12.12 and 3.14.6, including source/receipt corruption and relocation of the staged-file export. Selected-record integrity and patch application against refreshed main also pass. No full repository replay, Linux CI result, numerical exponential, physical tape-cost audit, or full multiplication proof is claimed.\n\n- Exact base: `47481c89fd30a43f8f882eb4b391e89c29273fd0`.\n- PR479 source: `40dd01058439cdffae3e3b41c4fe52edaccf5f91`; five original files preserved with Git-blob and SHA-256 pins.\n- All additions are confined to `research/chirp-symbolic-seed80/`; selected certificates and `upstream/` are unchanged.\n- Seed 80, independent-verification track. No pinned coordination issue exists; the claim is local. Final queue inspection found no overlapping symbolic PR479 check. #684, #940 and #481 concern distinct block-domain, layout and boundary-cost obligations.\n\nCredit to Chafik Boukhalfa's PR479 and its retained manuscript/analytic contributors. Prepared by Ross Richardson with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in research, code, verification and writing. Apache-2.0; no independent human peer review claimed.\n",
